      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T23:45:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t entirely correct. The client network needs to specify the remote MAC *and* PSM, while the server network technically doesn\u0027t specify any, it allocates / reserves the PSM.\n\n---\n\nHow about:\n\nThis specifier contains the information required to request a client L2CAP network using {@link ConnectivityManager#requestNetwork} and specifying the remote MAC address, Protocol/Service Multiplexer (PSM). It can also contain information allocated by the system when reserving a server network using {@link ConnectivityManager#reserveNetwork} such as the Protocol/Service Multiplexer (PSM). In both cases, the header compression option must always be specified.\n\n---\n\nReworded this section a bit. Thanks for the suggestions.",
      "parentUuid": "4f7c7c9d_46725052",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "a14d0b69159fe1e6a424c6665e8317bf1ac70ed3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
